Use io, list, and string.

Define function byte_at taking text as a pointer to TcString, index as an unsigned number returning a byte:
    Give back text.data[index].
Done.

Let first be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("flower"), bytes_len("flower")).
Let second be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("flow"), bytes_len("flow")).
Let third be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("flight"), bytes_len("flight")).
Let words be an empty list of text.
push first to address of words.
push second to address of words.
push third to address of words.
Let word_count be count of words.

Let shortest be list_get(address of words, 0).
Let limit be length of address of shortest.
For every w from 1 as an unsigned number to word_count - 1:
    Let word be list_get(address of words, w).
    Let word length be length of address of word.
    If word length is less than limit:
        Set limit to word length.

Let prefix_len start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Let matching be true.
Repeat while prefix_len is less than limit and matching is true:
    Let sample_byte be byte_at(address of first, prefix_len).
    For every w from 1 as an unsigned number to word_count - 1:
        Let word be list_get(address of words, w).
        If byte_at(address of word, prefix_len) isn't equal to sample_byte:
            Set matching to false.
    If matching is true:
        Add 1 to prefix_len.

Let prefix be create text from first.data of length prefix_len.
Say prefix.
str_free(address of prefix).
list_free(address of words).
str_free(address of third).
str_free(address of second).
str_free(address of first).
Return 0.
